  <!--
    ⚠️ Only the homepage is listed above on purpose.

    This app is a single-page app that routes with query strings
    (?page=..., ?product=...) rather than real paths like
    /algo-trading-bots/ or /forex-eas/. A sitemap entry only helps
    Google if the URL actually renders that content when crawled
    directly and is the canonical URL for it — right now none of the
    other pages/products have a dedicated path, so listing fake
    /algo-trading-bots/ style URLs here would be misleading and could
    hurt indexing rather than help it.

    To properly list products and categories here, you'd need one of:
      1) Real path-based routes (e.g. Vercel rewrites mapping
         /algo-trading-bots/ and /product/<id> to index.html, plus JS
         that reads the path instead of only the query string), or
      2) A small server/edge function that generates sitemap.xml from
         your Firebase product data on a schedule.
    Both are bigger changes than a safe drop-in fix, so they're left
    as a recommended next step rather than done automatically here.
  -->
